{"status":"confirmed","reasoning":"Relative to θ, the opposite side is 3, the adjacent side is 4, and the hypotenuse is 5. Thus csc θ = 5/3, sec θ = 5/4, and cot θ = 4/3. All three agree with Math Academy's worked solution.","confidence":1,"answers":[{"key":"solution","correct_value":"\\csc\\theta=\\frac{5}{3},\\quad\\sec\\theta=\\frac{5}{4},\\quad\\cot\\theta=\\frac{4}{3}","correct_option":null,"value_type":"math","wrong_value":"\\csc\\theta=\\frac{3}{5},\\quad\\sec\\theta=\\frac{4}{5},\\quad\\cot\\theta=\\frac{3}{4}","correct_keys":[],"wrong_keys":[],"ma_value":"\\csc\\theta=\\frac{5}{3},\\quad\\sec\\theta=\\frac{5}{4},\\quad\\cot\\theta=\\frac{4}{3}","ma_basis":"worked_solution","ma_evidence":"\\csc\\theta &= \\dfrac{1}{\\sin\\theta} = \\dfrac {\\text{hypotenuse}} {\\text{opposite}} = \\dfrac 5 3, \\[5pt]\n\t\t\\sec\\theta &= \\dfrac{1}{\\cos\\theta} =  \\dfrac {\\text{hypotenuse}} {\\text{adjacent}} = \\dfrac 5 4, \\[5pt]\n\t\t\\cot\\theta &= \\dfrac{1}{\\tan\\theta} = \\dfrac {\\text{adjacent}} {\\text{opposite}} = \\dfrac 4 3.","disagrees":false}]}